{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>Is it not hidden with Me, etc.</b> The meaning is: even though on account of the wrath of the enemy I refrained from executing upon them the judgment warranted by their deeds, for this reason they will not be exempt from the punishment coming to them — <b>is it not hidden with Me</b>, sealed in My treasuries for the day of judgment. Concerning this the prophet said (Isaiah 10:3): ״וּמַה תַּעֲשׂוּ לְיוֹם פְּקֻדָּה״, and go out and learn from what Samuel trembled from the fear of the day of judgment, as they said, of blessed memory (Ḥagigah 4b), in the incident of the mistress of the ov. And He doubled the expression, saying ״כָּמוּס עִמָּדִי חָתוּם״ and so forth, in the manner of His saying (Exodus 34:7) ״נוֹשֵׂא עָוֹן״; and when it reaches the point where He says ״נִלְאֵיתִי נְשׂוֹא״ (Isaiah 1:14), He will seal it in the treasuries and He Himself will take vengeance upon the perpetrators of wickedness by bringing the sun out of its sheath (Nedarim 8b), and it shall burn them, the day of YHWH, and this is His saying ״לִי נָקָם״ — meaning that He Himself will take vengeance, as it were."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:21:35.688482354Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}